    card title "How many chickens a year?"

A: How many chickens are killed for meat around the world every year? You and my co-host both get a guess.
    draw hen

    hide hen

    ask "Set your guess, in billions of chickens a year." estimate.min 1 estimate.max 1000 estimate.value 78 estimate.unit billion estimate.log true store g default "100" relative true tolerance 0.3
        right: Near enough: about seventy-eight billion chickens a year.
        wrong: The real count: about seventy-eight billion a year.

B: I put a hundred billion, so I overshot. But seventy-eight billion, with only eight billion people?
    highlight estimate_1

    erase estimate_1

A: Yes: that's nearly ten chickens for every person on Earth, every year.
    draw person r0 r1 r2 r3 r4 r5 r6 r7 r8 r9 pp parallel true

B: Ten? Then someone's been eating mine.
    highlight r0 r1 r2 r3 r4 r5 r6 r7 r8 r9

    erase person pp r0 r1 r2 r3 r4 r5 r6 r7 r8 r9

A: Some eat none, some far more. Counted per second, it's about two and a half thousand, day and night.
    draw clock ps ps2

    erase clock ps ps2

A: And it keeps climbing. In 1961 it was six and a half billion; now, twelve times as many.
    draw c61 l61 x12 g0 g1 g2 g3 g4 g5 g6 g7 g8 g9 g10 g11 lnow parallel true

    erase c61 l61 x12 lnow g0 g1 g2 g3 g4 g5 g6 g7 g8 g9 g10 g11

A: Of all the land animals killed for meat, about nine in ten are chickens.
    draw r0 r1 r2 r3 r4 r5 r6 r7 r8 q10 nine parallel true

B: And the tenth? Cows? Pigs?
    highlight q10

    erase q10

A: Mostly ducks. Pigs and cattle together are only about one in fifty.
    draw duck rare

B: So when we say farm animals, we really mean birds.
    highlight duck effect circle

